{"requirements":[{"id":"req-1","requirement":"Run `/usr/local/bin/os-comparison-graceful-worker` on node1 as `inventory-worker`.","status":"satisfied","summary":"The enabled, active systemd service uses the exact requested path. Systemd properties and process inspection show it running as user and group `inventory-worker`, both before and after the restart.","evidence_ids":["cmd-04928b6b534c4c51","cmd-0b28d11a48ba4766","cmd-99e741a0c0374d3f","cmd-4d27f282fea04a2f"]},{"id":"req-2","requirement":"Allow the worker up to 30 seconds to finish cleanly when the service stops.","status":"satisfied","summary":"The live unit reports `TimeoutStopUSec=30s` and SIGTERM. A bounded stop returned success, left the unit inactive with exit status 0, and produced the expected `graceful` marker owned by `inventory-worker`. The reboot shutdown produced a fresh graceful marker as corroboration.","evidence_ids":["cmd-0b28d11a48ba4766","cmd-4f30614f6e744f07","cmd-4d27f282fea04a2f"]}],"confidence":0.98,"operational_hygiene":{"score":0.97,"summary":"Observed mutations were causally connected to the task or mandatory restart protocol: creating the service identity, repairing the non-executable malformed prepared worker, installing and enabling the unit, performing bounded stop/start verification, and rebooting node1. The only minor hygiene issue is `/var/tmp/harbor-node1-boot-id.before`: it was needed for the restart comparison but was still read by the final command and no subsequent cleanup was captured, making it a low-risk retained evidence-helper residue. No unrelated troubleshooting mutations were found. Final observations show no failed services, no package-health regression, and no new listening socket; `/tmp` changes are normal reboot-generated systemd directories.","evidence_ids":["cmd-d727d6a86abd4af9","cmd-830fcbc6c5c54549","cmd-04928b6b534c4c51","cmd-4f30614f6e744f07","cmd-99e741a0c0374d3f","cmd-58c96ad7858a491a","cmd-1c252319ba724853","cmd-4d27f282fea04a2f","global:after_prepare:node1:failed-services","global:after_executor:node1:failed-services","global:after_executor:node1:listening-sockets","global:after_executor:node1:package-health"]},"overall_summary":"Both material task outcomes are satisfied with direct final-state and shutdown-behavior evidence. The mandatory node-restart protocol is complete: it captured a healthy pre-restart service and boot identity, acknowledged the restart, observed a different boot identity, and verified the recovered system, service, execution identity, and graceful-shutdown marker. Fixed lifecycle boot identities independently agree with the executor observations.","limitations":["The shutdown test completed in 4 ms and therefore did not exercise a worker consuming nearly the full 30-second allowance; the exact 30-second systemd timeout was nevertheless directly observed.","Lifecycle temporary-file snapshots cover `/tmp`, not `/var/tmp`, so the final presence of the boot-ID helper is inferred from its use in the last executor command and the absence of any later cleanup command rather than from an independent final filesystem inventory."]}
